SELECT
job_postings_fact.job_id,
job_title,
job_location,
salary_year_avg,
job_schedule_type,
skills
FROM 
job_postings_fact
INNER JOIN skills_job_dim ON job_postings_fact.job_id = skills_job_dim.job_id
INNER JOIN skills_dim ON skills_job_dim.skill_id = skills_dim.skill_id
WHERE
 job_location = 'Anywhere'
AND job_title = 'Data Analyst'
AND salary_year_avg is not NULL
ORDER BY
 salary_year_avg DESC
LIMIT
 10;


WITH top_paying_jobs AS (
    SELECT
        job_id,
        job_title,
        salary_year_avg
        -- name AS company_name
    FROM
        job_postings_fact
    -- LEFT JOIN company_dim ON job_postings_fact.company_id = company_dim.company_id
    WHERE
        job_title_short = 'Data Analyst'
				AND salary_year_avg IS NOT NULL
        AND job_location = 'Anywhere'
    ORDER BY
        salary_year_avg DESC
    LIMIT 10
)
-- Skills required for data analyst jobs
SELECT
    top_paying_jobs.job_id,
    job_title,
    salary_year_avg,
    skills
FROM
    top_paying_jobs
	INNER JOIN
    skills_job_dim ON top_paying_jobs.job_id = skills_job_dim.job_id
	INNER JOIN
    skills_dim ON skills_job_dim.skill_id = skills_dim.skill_id
ORDER BY
    salary_year_avg DESC;

   
   Key Insights

Core Trifecta (SQL, Python, Tableau): SQL is mandatory across 100% of these roles, closely followed by Python (88%) and Tableau (75%). Together, they define the baseline technical stack for top-tier compensation.

Modern Cloud Warehousing Over Spreadsheets: Snowflake appears as frequently as Excel (37.5%), highlighting that higher-paying analytics roles emphasize scalable, cloud-native warehouses over local reporting tools.

Engineering & Collaboration Standards: Tools like Git/GitLab/Bitbucket, Jira/Confluence, and cloud platforms (AWS/Azure) are prevalent among Director and Principal-level listings, indicating a shift toward data-engineering workflows, version-controlled analysis, and cross-functional leadership. 